<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#eze-nri">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eze Nri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eze Nri was the title of the priest-king of Nri, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igbo-people">Igbo</a> sacred kingdom in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. The Eze Nri held ritual rather than military authority: his agents travelled widely to cleanse abominations, settle disputes, crown titled men and bless the yam harvest. Tradition names Ifikuanim as the first holder, and the office survived, with diminished power, under British rule.</p></div>
